  "text": "The second thing adapters give us is, honestly, the bigger deal. Some qualities have no dataset to copy at all. Those Swiss apartments teach the model what a floor plan looks like they don't teach it what makes one good. There's no library of \"good\" lying around to copy. But here's the key insight: even when we can't show the model the right answer, we can SCORE the answer it gives us. So instead of \"copy this,\" the adapter learns from feedback here's the task, here's how you did, try again. And because it's an adapter, what it picks up that way combines with everything the imitation adapters already know. We score five things: does the room mix match the brief, do the rooms get daylight, is the circulation tight, does the furniture actually fit, and are the loads carried efficiently. One catch this loop runs millions of times, so every score has to come back in MILLISECONDS. If an evaluator's too slow, we make it fast. Which is exactly what we had to do for the structural check.",
